OL,3,GNEWSAWoman's lies led to innocent man's
OL,4,Adetention
OL,5,
OL,6,FHook, from Washington, admitted
OL,7,Fintending to pervert the course of
OL,8,Fjustice. Her two-year jail term was
OL,9,Fsuspended for two years after a
OL,10,Fpsychiatrist said her learning
OL,11,Fdifficulties and "emotional inadequacy"
OL,12,Fwere a factor in her offending.
